_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-p1[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Glossary panel with term-and-relation navigation, project cycling, [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]and add/delete[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A user drafting a prompt can press `gG` or `<ctrl+g>G` to open a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Glossary panel that browses one project's terms alphabetically, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]travels through related terms in both directions with a back trail,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cycles the visible project with `p`/`P`, and adds or deletes terms [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]through the same engine that backs the new `sase glossary add` and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sase glossary del` commands.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]glossary_panel.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared glossary add/delete engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mutation[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mutation: build the project-scoped glossary write engine that resolves a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]target project's config, validates a candidate entry set through the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Rust glossary validator, applies a source-preserving YAML insert or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]removal with an atomic stale-write guard, and returns a typed outcome [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]carrying diagnostics and a restore command; add the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reverse-reference index alongside it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase glossary add and del commands[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mutation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: register `add` and `del` in the alphabetically ordered glossary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]subcommand group, render rich and json outcomes, resolve `del` targets [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the existing alias/prefix lookup, print the restore command, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regenerate the project's agent instruction files in-process unless [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]suppressed, and extend shell completion and docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Multi-project glossary catalog service for the TUI[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mutation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog: add the ACE-side service that builds the ordered project ring [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for `p`/`P`, loads and compiles each project's glossary off the event [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]loop behind an mtime-keyed snapshot cache, exposes outbound and inbound [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation lists per entry, and invalidates cleanly after a write.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Glossary panel shell, term list, filter, and project ring[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel: factor the duplicated focused-scope keymap loaders into one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]generic loader, declare the `glossary` keymap scope and every panel [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]action up front, then build the modal shell with its header, filterable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]term list, definition card, footer, and `p`/`P` project cycling over the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ring.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Related-term travel, relation chips, and the back trail[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]travel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]travel: render numbered SEE ALSO and REFERENCED BY chip rows on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]definition card, add the chip cursor, digit shortcuts, follow and back [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keys, and the bounded breadcrumb trail that keeps the term list [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection synchronized with every jump.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Panel add and delete surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]actions[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mutation, panel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]actions: add the term-add form with live validation, the delete [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirmation that shows the inbound blast radius, tracked-proc writes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the shared engine, the post-write commit offer, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]optimistic reselect-and-refresh behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prompt keymap entry point and focus handoff[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]entry[dim] · [dim][/dim]after travel, actions[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry: claim `G` on the prompt `g` prefix table so `gG` and `<ctrl+g>G` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both open the panel with a hint row, post the open request as a message [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the app handles, seed the selection from the glossary term under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cursor, and restore prompt focus and vim mode on close.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Help, docs, and visual snapshots[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]polish[dim] · [dim]